somehow i expected the dominar line area to be more dominating i regret to dampen spirits but

00:28:52.240 --> 00:28:59.650
pilot reports a problem my scans show that the bit screen is not fully complete there are gaps which

00:29:00.250 --> 00:29:01.010
vulnerable.

00:29:01.810 --> 00:29:10.650
The DS is overlaid on top of one another.

00:29:11.660 --> 00:29:13.600
We only had time to hook up one.

00:29:14.060 --> 00:29:15.000
Whoa, whoa, whoa, wait a minute.

00:29:17.210 --> 00:29:18.270
How crazy is this?

00:29:18.370 --> 00:29:19.330
Now, there's two systems, right?

00:29:19.940 --> 00:29:20.220
Yeah.

00:29:20.800 --> 00:29:22.600
So why don't we install one of them on Moyet?

00:29:27.860 --> 00:29:29.980
I have been sworn never to con-

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:32.420
Compromise peacekeeper technology with the enemy.

00:29:32.700 --> 00:29:49.200
I will do it for you. For all of you.

00:29:53.260 --> 00:29:58.240
To displace an overlord during battle and then fail?

00:30:00.160 --> 00:30:11.250
not my fault. What about my father? You only cracks your father. This is on you. Choose.

00:30:15.180 --> 00:30:23.900
Lead my unit and capture that ship with no prisoners taken. Those gaps in the protective

00:30:23.900 --> 00:30:29.980
barrier you must fly through are small and shifting. Do you leave me a...

00:30:35.150 --> 00:30:40.320
Perhaps one day they will sing songs of your early death.

00:30:43.060 --> 00:30:46.570
So you like deep space physics too?

00:30:47.090 --> 00:30:50.250
Yeah. You know cosmic theory?

00:30:51.840 --> 00:30:53.640
Yeah, it's something that intrigues me.

00:30:56.520 --> 00:30:57.740
I got my doctorate in it.

00:30:57.880 --> 00:30:59.190
Oh, sorry.

00:31:00.440 --> 00:31:01.220
What is that?

00:31:01.420 --> 00:31:04.400
It's a couple of letters they added into your name.

00:31:05.850 --> 00:31:07.050
Not much help out here, though.

00:31:07.770 --> 00:31:15.000
Last textbook I read made a case for why you and all other forms of alien life didn't exist.

00:31:18.040 --> 00:31:21.290
Can you, um, can you anchor this while I pull?

00:31:24.870 --> 00:31:27.190
Hold that. Got it?

00:31:27.330 --> 00:31:27.730
Yeah, go.

00:31:38.920 --> 00:31:44.900
It seems human civilization men are much the same.

00:31:47.300 --> 00:31:48.900
I don't notice any difference in the women either.

00:32:37.710 --> 00:32:42.500
I've set up four of the components in the maintenance bay.

00:33:00.890 --> 00:33:02.110
Aaron, would you wait?

00:33:04.040 --> 00:33:05.660
What the heck's the matter with you?

00:33:06.320 --> 00:33:08.760
I'm sure you can see how heavy these things are.

00:33:08.860 --> 00:33:10.280
There's at least another ten in there.

00:33:10.420 --> 00:33:12.440
Do not come down this corridor without one.

00:33:14.550 --> 00:33:15.750
Would you stop?

00:33:19.110 --> 00:33:20.850
Okay, what happened back there was...

00:33:20.850 --> 00:33:21.690
None of my business.

00:33:22.090 --> 00:33:23.390
Yes, it was.

00:33:23.910 --> 00:33:29.960
You and I are shipmates trying to save...

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:37.720
is haven't you just clicked with a guy what clicked yeah you know found a guy attractive

00:33:37.720 --> 00:33:49.220
yes but i didn't let it in the beginning i found you interesting me yes but only for a moment

00:33:49.220 --> 00:33:58.830
good good i mean it's good to be on even terms i agree

00:34:02.330 --> 00:34:05.860
Yeah, so this is a good idea to clear the air.

00:34:55.790 --> 00:34:56.960
Dukker, you?

00:35:08.640 --> 00:35:11.460
You once told me I would never leave your ship alive.

00:35:12.990 --> 00:35:14.900
You're weary of so many cycles.

00:35:16.500 --> 00:35:17.620
No matter what you did to me,

00:35:18.480 --> 00:35:20.140
I'll always remember one thing.

00:35:33.060 --> 00:35:34.760
Separation from the main module.

00:35:35.370 --> 00:35:36.570
Launch the others.

00:35:45.930 --> 00:35:48.030
They're moving too fast to track them all.

00:35:52.080 --> 00:35:55.040
When they get aboard the Zalbinium, can they breach the defense screen?

00:35:55.480 --> 00:35:59.970
When I kill the Bypass, these two Polaro discs will be attracted to it.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:06.080
each other strongly so you have to hold them apart because if they touch each other this whole room

00:36:06.080 --> 00:36:17.770
will be vaporized foragers it's time to prove our glory have any of them made it through i can't tell

00:36:17.770 --> 00:36:24.040
yet i'll have to do a debris analysis quickly aim for the gaps in the defense screen

00:36:45.320 --> 00:36:47.190
Maintenance, babe. What's the problem?

00:36:47.450 --> 00:36:50.210
We think one of the Shi Yangs got on board the Zalbinian.

00:36:52.990 --> 00:36:54.070
How the hell did that happen?

00:36:54.390 --> 00:36:55.090
Not important.

00:36:55.620 --> 00:36:57.580
What is, is he may be heading right toward you.

00:37:03.360 --> 00:37:04.140
You gotta stop.

00:37:04.460 --> 00:37:06.060
Not once I've stopped the process.

00:37:06.480 --> 00:37:07.700
Then finish the process.

00:37:08.360 --> 00:37:12.030
I'm working as fast as I can.

00:37:12.170 --> 00:37:13.170
I want you to get out of here.

00:37:13.250 --> 00:37:14.410
I won't leave you.

00:37:44.200 --> 00:37:50.350
You die here to me. I die too.

00:38:00.700 --> 00:38:03.960
She keeps blocking my room, forcing me to take the long way around.

00:38:04.450 --> 00:38:05.190
You may have...

00:38:06.110 --> 00:38:09.130
Look, Aaron, it's a long story, but I kind of got my hands full here,

00:38:09.170 --> 00:38:10.750
so you're going to have to get here.

00:38:22.860 --> 00:38:24.440
Spongy's inside the door right now.

00:38:32.490 --> 00:38:33.170
Aaron's gonna get here.

00:38:42.960 --> 00:38:43.560
Spit fire?

00:38:44.780 --> 00:38:46.220
How come nobody tells me they're studs?

00:38:46.240 --> 00:38:47.800
How come nobody tells me they spit fire?

00:38:47.940 --> 00:38:48.220
Aaron!

00:39:11.100 --> 00:39:15.200
Look, as you can see, it's not likely we're going to hurt you, so just take anything you want.

00:39:15.280 --> 00:39:16.900
But if these two paddles touch...

00:39:25.500 --> 00:39:26.380
Listen, gasshole!

00:39:27.060 --> 00:39:29.040
You kill us, you kill yourself!

00:39:29.320 --> 00:39:29.960
You hagg-

00:39:30.060 --> 00:39:31.360
your chance to retreat.

00:39:31.780 --> 00:39:34.350
Come a little closer then.

00:39:34.550 --> 00:39:36.370
Let's just find out what happens when these battles

00:39:36.370 --> 00:39:36.670
start.

00:40:01.080 --> 00:40:02.320
Sorry about the mess.

00:40:12.510 --> 00:40:13.390
Absolutely not.

00:40:13.730 --> 00:40:15.730
Our situation is untenable as it is.

00:40:15.910 --> 00:40:17.090
I'm with Dargo on this, John.

00:40:17.850 --> 00:40:21.050
Allowing Jelena to encourage Grace's return is suicidal and best.

00:40:21.230 --> 00:40:25.090
Look, the Shiangs are sitting out there waiting for another chance to slip through.

00:40:25.270 --> 00:40:27.530
And Grace is going to come back one day.

00:40:28.490 --> 00:40:29.010
What then?

00:40:29.280 --> 00:40:29.980
We have done well.

00:40:30.600 --> 00:40:32.580
Crace as it is. With a start,

00:40:32.760 --> 00:40:34.040
he would soon catch us.

00:40:34.560 --> 00:40:37.300
Not if she doesn't tell him we were here.

00:40:38.830 --> 00:40:40.390
I'm a trusting soul at best,

00:40:40.470 --> 00:40:41.850
but not to a fault.

00:40:43.950 --> 00:40:45.610
The tech will not reveal our presence.

00:40:46.880 --> 00:40:48.580
How can you be so sure about that?

00:40:49.350 --> 00:40:52.090
You know what happened to me, being deemed

00:40:52.090 --> 00:40:54.270
irreversibly contaminated by Crace,

00:40:55.140 --> 00:40:57.240
contamination by enemy lifeforms.

00:40:58.360 --> 00:40:59.640
That could happen to you.

00:41:01.630 --> 00:41:05.730
Punishment is death, or worse, banishment.

00:41:05.970 --> 00:41:14.000
I hope you will only ever imagine how horrible it is to never return to the life that you love.

00:41:18.410 --> 00:41:20.820
You are smarter than that, Jelena.

00:41:26.680 --> 00:41:29.760
I've sent a distress call to the Peacekeeper carrier.

00:41:30.380 --> 00:41:31.600
I passed through here earlier.

00:41:32.860 --> 00:41:35.360
It is returning at maximum speed.

00:41:35.840 --> 00:41:37.840
Any word from Lomus?

00:41:38.480 --> 00:41:41.720
His life signal is no longer active.

00:41:42.180 --> 00:41:46.530
What do you think we should do, Wevran?

00:41:47.820 --> 00:41:49.100
I'm sorry you were leaving.

00:41:49.700 --> 00:41:52.440
My officers are drawing up plans to retaliate.

00:41:52.600 --> 00:41:53.800
I doubt so.

00:41:54.960 --> 00:41:56.080
You had nothing.

00:41:57.300 --> 00:41:59.150
But you, you will.

00:42:00.510 --> 00:42:05.360
Evran, there is no shame in losing to a clever opponent.

00:42:06.800 --> 00:42:16.270
And Cardago, point to someday kill my clever opponent.

00:42:23.700 --> 00:42:25.060
You are magnificent, Dago.

00:42:26.000 --> 00:42:27.560
With or without your assistance.

00:42:28.840 --> 00:42:29.460
In spite of it.

00:42:33.680 --> 00:42:35.120
Grace will ask you many questions.

00:42:41.490 --> 00:42:42.590
I wish I had been so smart.

00:43:23.610 --> 00:43:24.290
this weekend.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:48.420
overhaul a prowler engine but apart from that yes julina i don't want you to go are you asking

00:43:48.420 --> 00:43:56.710
me to stay no i can't i can't this is no way to live i can't ask you to come back with me because

00:43:58.200 --> 00:43:59.300
grace would kill you

00:44:06.120 --> 00:44:12.140
So what do we do?

00:44:16.270 --> 00:44:22.250
We're going to see you again, am I?

00:44:23.080 --> 00:44:23.860
Oh, yes.

00:44:24.660 --> 00:44:25.620
We'll find a way.

00:44:25.740 --> 00:44:29.630
We'll organize a rendezvous point for later or something.

00:44:30.860 --> 00:44:31.280
something.

00:44:35.560 --> 00:44:37.260
Time must go.

00:44:37.850 --> 00:44:38.650
In a minute, Dargo.

00:44:53.910 --> 00:44:54.490
Us together.

00:46:26.520 --> 00:46:27.700
I shall never understand.

00:46:28.600 --> 00:46:29.620
It's kind of all purpose.

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:32.460
other person decide what they want to talk about.

00:46:32.940 --> 00:46:34.100
What if they don't want to talk?

00:46:35.160 --> 00:46:36.420
Then they say hey back.

00:46:37.580 --> 00:46:44.190
Well now the first person that doesn't want to talk

00:46:44.190 --> 00:46:45.850
can be trumped if the

00:46:45.850 --> 00:46:47.650
other person realizes that they need to.

00:46:49.480 --> 00:46:49.640
Hey.

00:47:00.220 --> 00:47:01.600
I hate being ambushed.

00:47:03.520 --> 00:47:05.620
Well, you got him in the end. That's all that counts.

00:47:05.900 --> 00:47:09.150
I wasn't talking about the Shiangs.

00:47:13.940 --> 00:47:19.260
You know, in my world, they say that loss is the hardest emotion to deal with.

00:47:19.360 --> 00:47:21.820
In my world, showing pain is a sign of weakness.

00:47:23.750 --> 00:47:25.350
How can you not feel pain after what you've been through?

00:47:26.190 --> 00:47:27.650
Don't presume you'll understand me, John.

00:47:30.320 --> 00:47:33.880
That's not fair. It's not fair, Aaron.

00:47:34.560 --> 00:47:36.680
You bash me all the time for being soft.

00:47:36.840 --> 00:47:38.780
Well, the fact of the matter is that sometimes it's an advantage,

00:47:38.800 --> 00:47:40.520
and this is one of them. I think I understand you.

00:47:40.960 --> 00:47:42.520
There's no way you can know how I feel.

00:47:45.720 --> 00:47:50.650
If I somehow, someday get a chance to return to my world,

00:47:51.580 --> 00:47:52.900
walk around my old neighborhood,

00:47:54.130 --> 00:47:58.400
see my old house, dad's truck, best friend's bike on the lawn,

00:47:58.400 --> 00:47:59.900
and then I get a chance to go...

00:48:00.760 --> 00:48:09.020
inside. I walked through the living room upstairs to my room. I had a poster of Clint Eastwood,

00:48:10.830 --> 00:48:25.480
good, the bad, and the ugly. And then I think, if everyone were dead, if all my friends

00:48:25.480 --> 00:48:27.820
and family were lying there dead.

00:48:32.750 --> 00:48:34.290
Oh, what would it be like to go home then?

00:48:39.680 --> 00:48:40.420
I stand corrected.
